WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.404 --> 00:00:03.460
Unit twenty-one. Social Engineering!

2
00:00:04.444 --> 00:00:09.006
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.056 --> 00:00:12.530
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.588
Today we learn about Social Engineering. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.146 --> 00:00:23.279
Social engineering. Say it with me. Social engineering!

6
00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:30.077
Trick. Say it with me. Trick!

7
00:00:33.502 --> 00:00:36.969
Trust. Say it with me. Trust!

8
00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:44.230
Pretend. Say it with me. Pretend!

9
00:00:47.785 --> 00:00:51.318
Urgent. Say it with me. Urgent!

10
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:58.516
Password. Say it with me. Password!

11
00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:06.007
Verify. Say it with me. Verify!

12
00:01:09.499 --> 00:01:13.116
Report. Say it with me. Report!

13
00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:29.295
Social engineering is when attackers trick people instead of hacking computers. They pretend to be someone you trust and create an urgent feeling. Always verify requests and never share a password.

14
00:01:29.345 --> 00:01:32.747
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:33.487 --> 00:01:38.616
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:38.666 --> 00:01:39.816
Trust!

17
00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:46.118
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.168 --> 00:01:47.318
Verify!

19
00:01:48.319 --> 00:01:54.314
Did you know? Many cyberattacks start by tricking a person rather than breaking technology!

20
00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:56.644
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:06.543
Think and answer. How might someone use social engineering at school?

22
00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:07.743
Great answer!

23
00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:13.924
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:13.974 --> 00:02:17.025
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

